#| msgid "KDE Software Compilation 4.11 Beta1"
msgid "December 16, 2015. Today KDE released KDE Applications 15.12."
msgstr "KDE-Software-Tosamenstellen 4.11 Beta 1"

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:7
msgid ""
"KDE is excited to announce the release of KDE Applications 15.12, the "
"December 2015 update to KDE Applications. This release brings one new "
"application and feature additions and bug fixes across the board to existing "
"applications. The team strives to always bring the best quality to your "
"desktop and these applications, so we're counting on you to send your "
"feedback."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:9
msgid ""
"In this release, we've updated a whole host of applications to use the new "
"<a href='%[1]s'>KDE Frameworks 5</a>, including <a href='%[2]s'>Artikulate</"
"a>, <a href='%[3]s'>Krfb</a>, <a href='%[4]s'>KSystemLog</a>, <a "
"href='https://games.kde.org/game.php?game=klickety'>Klickety</a> and more of "
"the KDE Games, apart from the KDE Image Plugin Interface and its support "
"libraries. This brings the total number of applications that use KDE "
"Frameworks 5 to 126."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:11
msgid "A Spectacular New Addition"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:13
msgid ""
"After 14 years of being a part of KDE, KSnapshot has been retired and "
"replaced with a new screenshot application, Spectacle."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:15
msgid ""
"With new features and a completely new UI, Spectacle makes taking "
"screenshots as easy and unobtrusive as it can ever be. In addition to what "
"you could do with KSnapshot, with Spectacle you can now take composite "
"screenshots of pop-up menus along with their parent windows, or take "
"screenshots of the entire screen (or the currently active window) without "
"even starting Spectacle, simply by using the keyboard shortcuts Shift"
"+PrintScreen and Meta+PrintScreen respectively."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:17
msgid ""
"We've also aggressively optimised application start-up time, to absolutely "
"minimise the time lag between when you start the application and when the "
"image is captured."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:19
msgid "Polish Everywhere"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:21
msgid ""
"Many of the applications have undergone significant polishing in this cycle, "
"in addition to stability and bug fixes."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:23
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>Kdenlive</a>, the non-linear video editor, has seen major "
"fixes to its User Interface. You can now copy and paste items on your "
"timeline, and easily toggle transparency in a given track. The icon colours "
"automatically adjust to the main UI theme, making them easier to see."
msgstr ""

#. type: shortcode parameter
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:25
msgid "Ark can now show ZIP comments"
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:27
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>Ark</a>, the archive manager, can now display comments "
"embedded in ZIP and RAR archives. We've improved support for Unicode "
"characters in file names in ZIP archives, and you can now detect corrupt "
"archives and recover as much data as possible from them. You can also open "
"archived files in their default application, and we've fixed drag-and-drop "
"to the desktop as well previews for XML files."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:29
msgid "All Play and No Work"
msgstr ""

#. type: shortcode parameter
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:31
msgid "KSudoku new Welcome Screen (on a Mac OS X)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:33
msgid ""
"The KDE Games developers have been working hard for the past few months to "
"optimise our games for a smoother and richer experience, and we've got a lot "
"of new stuff in this area for our users to enjoy."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:35
msgid ""
"In <a href='%[1]s'>KGoldrunner</a>, we've added two new sets of levels, one "
"allowing digging while falling and one not. We've added solutions for "
"several existing sets of levels. For an added challenge, we now disallow "
"digging while falling in some older sets of levels."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:37
msgid ""
"In <a href='%[1]s'>KSudoku</a>, you can now print Mathdoku and Killer Sudoku "
"puzzles. The new multi-column layout in KSudoku's Welcome Screen makes it "
"easier to see more of the many puzzle types available, and the columns "
"adjust themselves automatically as the window is resized. We've done the "
"same to Palapeli, making it easier to see more of your jigsaw puzzle "
"collection at once."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:39
msgid ""
"We've also included stability fixes for games like KNavalBattle, Klickety, "
"<a href='%[1]s'>KShisen</a> and <a href='%[2]s'>KTuberling</a>, and the "
"overall experience is now greatly improved. KTuberling, Klickety and "
"KNavalBattle have also been updated to use the new KDE Frameworks 5."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:41
msgid "Important Fixes"
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:43
msgid ""
"Don't you simply hate it when your favorite application crashes at the most "
"inconvinient time? We do too, and to remedy that we've worked very hard at "
"fixing lots of bugs for you, but probably we've left some sneak, so don't "
"forget to <a href='%[1]s'>report them</a>!"
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:45
msgid ""
"In our file manager <a href='%[1]s'>Dolphin</a>, we've included various "
"fixes for stability and some fixes to make scrolling smoother. In <a "
"href='%[2]s'>Kanagram</a>, we've fixed a bothersome issue with white text on "
"white backgrounds. In <a href='%[3]s'>Kate</a>, we've attempted to fix a "
"crash that was occurring on shutdown, in addition to cleaning up the UI and "
"adding in a new cache cleaner."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:47
msgid ""
"The <a href='%[1]s'>Kontact Suite</a> has seen tons of added features, big "
"fixes and performance optimisations. In fact, there's been so much "
"development this cycle that we've bumped the version number to 5.1. The team "
"is hard at work, and is looking forward to all your feedback."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:49
msgid "Moving Forward"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:51
msgid ""
"As part of the effort to modernise our offerings, we've dropped some "
"applications from KDE Applications and are no longer releasing them as of "
"KDE Applications 15.12"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:53
msgid ""
"We've dropped 4 applications from the release - Amor, KTux, KSnapshot and "
"SuperKaramba. As noted above, KSnapshot has been replaced by Spectacle, and "
"Plasma essentially replaces SuperKaramba as a widget engine. We've dropped "
"standalone screensavers because screen locking is handled very differently "
"in modern desktops."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/15.12.0.md:55
msgid ""
"We've also dropped 3 artwork packages (kde-base-artwork, kde-wallpapers and "
"kdeartwork); their content had not changed in long time."
msgstr ""

