"impressive array of upgrades when it comes to better ease of access, the "
"introduction of highly useful functionalities and getting rid of some minor "
"issues, bringing KDE Applications one step closer to offering you the "
"perfect setup for your device."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/16.08.0.md:7
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>Kolourpaint</a>, <a href='%[2]s'>Cervisia</a> and KDiskFree "
"have now been ported to KDE Frameworks 5 and we look forward to your "
"feedback and insight into the newest features introduced with this release."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/16.08.0.md:9
msgid ""
"In the continued effort to split Kontact Suite libraries to make them easier "
"to use for third parties, the kdepimlibs tarball has been split into akonadi-"
"contacts, akonadi-mime and akonadi-notes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/16.08.0.md:11
msgid ""
"We have discontinued the following packages: kdegraphics-strigi-analyzer, "
"kdenetwork-strigi-analyzers, kdesdk-strigi-analyzers, libkdeedu and "
"mplayerthumbs. This will help us focus in the rest of the code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/announcements/applications/16.08.0.md:13
msgid "Keeping in Kontact"
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/16.08.0.md:15
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>The Kontact Suite</a> has got the usual round of cleanups, "
"bug fixes and optimizations in this release. Notable is the use of "
"QtWebEngine in various compontents, which allows for a more modern HTML "
"rendering engine to be used. We have also improved VCard4 support as well as "
"added new plugins that can warn if some conditions are met when sending an "
"email, e.g. verifying that you want to allow sending emails with a given "
"identity, or checking if you are sending email as plaintext, etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/announcements/applications/16.08.0.md:17
msgid "New Marble version"
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/16.08.0.md:19
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>Marble</a> 2.0 is part of KDE Applications 16.08 and "
"includes more than 450 code changes including improvements in navigation, "
"rendering and an experimental vector rendering of OpenStreetMap data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/announcements/applications/16.08.0.md:21
msgid "More Archiving"
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/16.08.0.md:23
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>Ark</a> can now extract AppImage and .xar files as well as "
"testing the integrity of zip, 7z and rar archives. It can also add/edit "
"comments in rar archives"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/announcements/applications/16.08.0.md:25
msgid "Terminal Improvements"
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/16.08.0.md:27
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>Konsole</a> has had improvements regarding font rendering "
"options and accessibility support."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/16.08.0.md:31
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>Kate</a> got movable tabs. <a href='%[2]s'>More "
"information...</a>"
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/16.08.0.md:33
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>KGeography</a>, has added provinces and regions maps of "
"Burkina Faso."
msgstr ""

