#. type: Title ##
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:9
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "KDE Software Compilation 4.11 Beta1"
msgid "What's new in KDE Applications 18.04"
msgstr "KDE-Software-Tosamenstellen 4.11 Beta 1"

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:15
msgid ""
"The first major release in 2018 of <a href='%[1]s'>Dolphin</a>, KDE's "
"powerful file manager, features many improvements to its panels:"
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:17
msgid ""
"The 'Places' panel's sections can now be hidden if you prefer not to display "
"them, and a new 'Network' section is now available to hold entries for "
"remote locations."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:18
msgid ""
"The 'Terminal' panel can be docked to any side of the window, and if you try "
"to open it without Konsole installed, Dolphin will show a warning and help "
"you install it."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:19
msgid "HiDPI support for the 'Information' panel has been improved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:21
msgid "The folder view and the menus have been updated as well:"
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:23
msgid "The Trash folder now displays an 'Empty Trash' button."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:24
msgid ""
"A 'Show Target' menu item has been added to help finding symlink targets."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:25
msgid ""
"Git integration has been enhanced, as the context menu for git folders now "
"displays two new actions for 'git log' and 'git merge'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:27
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:47
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:100
msgid "Further improvements include:"
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:29
msgid ""
"A new shortcut has been introduced giving you the option to open the Filter "
"Bar simply by hitting the slash (/) key."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:30
msgid "You can now sort and organize photos by the date they were taken."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:31
msgid ""
"The drag-and-drop of many small files within Dolphin became faster, and "
"users can now undo batch rename jobs."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:35
msgid ""
"To make working on the command line even more enjoyable, <a "
"href='%[1]s'>Konsole</a>, KDE's terminal emulator application, can now look "
"prettier:"
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:37
msgid "You can download color schemes via KNewStuff."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:38
msgid "The scrollbar blends in better with the active color scheme."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:39
msgid "By default the tab bar is shown only when needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:41
msgid ""
"Konsole's contributors did not stop there, and introduced many new features:"
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:43
msgid ""
"A new read-only mode and a profile property to toggle copying text as HTML "
"have been added."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:44
msgid "Under Wayland, Konsole now supports the drag-and-drop menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:45
msgid ""
"Several improvements took place in regards to the ZMODEM protocol: Konsole "
"can now handle the zmodem upload indicator B01, it will show the progress "
"while transferring data, the Cancel button in the dialog now works as it "
"should, and transferring of bigger files is better supported by reading them "
"into memory in 1MB chunks."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:49
msgid ""
"Mouse wheel scrolling with libinput has been fixed, and cycling through "
"shell history when scrolling with the mouse wheel is now prevented."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:50
msgid ""
"Searches are refreshed after changing the search match regular expression "
"option and when pressing 'Ctrl' + 'Backspace' Konsole will match xterm "
"behaviour."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:51
msgid "The '--background-mode' shortcut has been fixed."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:55
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>JuK</a>, KDE's music player, now has Wayland support. New UI "
"features include the ability to hide the menu bar and having a visual "
"indication of the currently playing track. While docking to the system tray "
"is disabled, JuK will no longer crash when attempting to quit via the window "
"'close' icon and the user interface will remain visible. Bugs regarding JuK "
"autoplaying unexpectedly when resuming from sleep in Plasma 5 and handling "
"the playlist column have also been fixed."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:57
msgid ""
"For the 18.04 release, contributors of <a href='%[1]s'>Kdenlive</a>, KDE's "
"non-linear video editor, focused on maintenance:"
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:59
msgid "Clip resizing no longer corrupts fades and keyframes."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:60
msgid "Users of display scaling on HiDPI monitors can enjoy crisper icons."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:61
msgid "A possible crash on startup with some configurations has been fixed."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:62
msgid ""
"MLT is now required to have version 6.6.0 or later, and compatibility is "
"improved."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:68
msgid ""
"Over the last months, contributors of <a href='%[1]s'>Gwenview</a>, KDE's "
"image viewer and organizer, worked on a plethora of improvements. Highlights "
"include:"
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:70
msgid ""
"Support for MPRIS controllers has been added so you can now control full "
"screen slideshows via KDE Connect, your keyboard's media keys, and the Media "
"Player plasmoid."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:71
msgid "The thumbnail hover buttons can now be turned off."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:72
msgid ""
"The Crop tool received several enhancements, as its settings are now "
"remembered when switching to another image, the shape of the selection box "
"can now be locked by holding down the 'Shift' or 'Ctrl' keys and it can also "
"be locked to the aspect ratio of the currently displayed image."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:73
msgid ""
"In full screen mode, you can now exit by using the 'Escape' key and the "
"color palette will reflect your active color theme. If you quit Gwenview in "
"this mode, this setting will be remembered and the new session will start in "
"full screen as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:75
msgid ""
"Attention to detail is important, so Gwenview has been polished in the "
"following areas:"
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:77
msgid ""
"Gwenview will display more human-readable file paths in the 'Recent Folders' "
"list, show the proper context menu for items in the 'Recent Files' list, and "
"correctly forget everything when using the 'Disable History' feature."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:78
msgid ""
"Clicking on a folder in the sidebar allows toggling between Browse and View "
"modes and remembers the last used mode when switching between folders, thus "
"allowing faster navigation in huge image collections."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:79
msgid ""
"Keyboard navigation has been further streamlined by properly indicating "
"keyboard focus in Browse mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:80
msgid ""
"The 'Fit Width' feature has been replaced with a more generalized 'Fill' "
"function."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:84
msgid ""
"Even smaller enhancements often can make user's workflows more enjoyable:"
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:86
msgid ""
"To improve consistency, SVG images are now enlarged like all other images "
"when 'Image View → Enlarge Smaller Images' is turned on."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:87
msgid ""
"After editing an image or undoing changes, image view and thumbnail won't "
"get out of sync anymore."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:88
msgid ""
"When renaming images, the filename extension will be unselected by default "
"and the 'Move/Copy/Link' dialog now defaults to showing the current folder."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:89
msgid ""
"Lots of visual papercuts were fixed, e.g. in the URL bar, for the full "
"screen toolbar, and for the thumbnail tooltip animations. Missing icons were "
"added as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:90
msgid ""
"Last but not least, the full screen hover button will directly view the "
"image instead of showing the folder's content, and the advanced settings now "
"allow for more control over the ICC color rendering intent."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:94
msgid ""
"In <a href='%[1]s'>Okular</a>, KDE's universal document viewer, PDF "
"rendering and text extraction can now be cancelled if you have poppler "
"version 0.63 or higher, which means that if you have a complex PDF file and "
"you change the zoom while it's rendering it will cancel immediately instead "
"of waiting for the render to finish."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:96
msgid ""
"You will find improved PDF JavaScript support for AFSimple_Calculate, and if "
"you have poppler version 0.64 or higher, Okular will support PDF JavaScript "
"changes in read-only state of forms."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:98
msgid ""
"Management of booking confirmation emails in <a href='%[1]s'>KMail</a>, "
"KDE's powerful email client, has been significantly enhanced to support "
"train bookings and uses a Wikidata-based airport database for showing "
"flights with correct timezone information. To make things easier for you, a "
"new extractor has been implemented for emails not containing structured "
"booking data."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:102
msgid "The message structure can again be shown with the new 'Expert' plugin."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:103
msgid ""
"A plugin has been added in the Sieve Editor for selecting emails from the "
"Akonadi database."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:104
msgid ""
"The text search in the editor has been improved with regular expression "
"support."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:110
msgid ""
"Improving the user interface of <a href='%[1]s'>Spectacle</a>, KDE's "
"versatile screenshot tool, was a major focus area:"
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:112
msgid ""
"The bottom row of buttons has received an overhaul, and now displays a "
"button to open the Settings window and a new 'Tools' button that reveals "
"methods to open the last-used screenshot folder and launch a screen "
"recording program."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:113
msgid "The last-used save mode is now remembered by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:114
msgid ""
"The window size now adapts to the aspect ratio of the screenshot, resulting "
"in a more pleasant and space-efficient screenshot thumbnail."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:115
msgid "The Settings window has been substantially simplified."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:117
msgid ""
"In addition, users will be able to simplify their workflows with these new "
"features:"
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:119
msgid ""
"When a specific window has been captured, its title can be automatically "
"added to the name of the screenshot file."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:120
msgid ""
"The user can now choose whether or not Spectacle automatically quits after "
"any save or copy operation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:122
msgid "Important bug fixes include:"
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:124
msgid "Drag-and-drop to Chromium windows now works as expected."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:125
msgid ""
"Repeatedly using the keyboard shortcuts to save a screenshot does not result "
"in an ambiguous shortcut warning dialog anymore."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:126
msgid ""
"For rectangular region screenshots, the bottom edge of the selection can be "
"adjusted more accurately."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:127
msgid ""
"Improved reliability of capturing windows touching screen edges when "
"compositing is turned off."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:131
msgid ""
"With <a href='%[1]s'>Kleopatra</a>, KDE's certificate manager and universal "
"crypto GUI, Curve 25519 EdDSA keys can be generated when used with a recent "
"version of GnuPG. A 'Notepad' view has been added for text based crypto "
"actions and you can now sign/encrypt and decrypt/verify directly in the "
"application. Under the 'Certificate details' view you will now find an "
"export action, which you can use to export as text to copy and paste. What's "
"more, you can import the result via the new 'Notepad' view."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:133
msgid ""
"In <a href='%[1]s'>Ark</a>, KDE's graphical file compression/decompression "
"tool with support for multiple formats, it is now possible to stop "
"compressions or extractions while using the libzip backend for ZIP archives."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:135
msgid "Applications joining the KDE Applications release schedule"
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:137
msgid ""
"KDE's webcam recorder <a href='%[1]s'>Kamoso</a> and backup program <a "
"href='%[2]s'>KBackup</a> will now follow the Applications releases. The "
"instant messenger <a href='%[3]s'>Kopete</a> is also being reintroduced "
"after being ported to KDE Frameworks 5."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:141
msgid ""
"The hex editor <a href='%[1]s'>Okteta</a> will have its own release schedule "
"after a request from its maintainer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.0.md:145
msgid ""
"More than 170 bugs have been resolved in applications including the Kontact "
"Suite, Ark, Dolphin, Gwenview, K3b, Kate, Kdenlive, Konsole, Okular, "
"Umbrello and more!"
msgstr ""

#: content/announcements/applications/18.04.1.md:0
