#| msgid "KDE Software Compilation 4.11 Beta1"
msgid ""
"The KDE community is happy to announce the release of KDE Applications %[1]s."
msgstr "KDE-Software-Tosamenstellen 4.11 Beta 1"

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:11
msgid ""
"Our community continuously works on improving the software included in our "
"KDE Application series. Along with new features, we improve the design, "
"usability and stability of all our utilities, games, and creativity tools. "
"Our aim is to make your life easier by making KDE software more enjoyable to "
"use. We hope you like all the new enhancements and bug fixes you'll find in "
"%[1]s!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:15
msgid ""
"More than 150 bugs have been resolved. These fixes re-implement disabled "
"features, normalize shortcuts, and solve crashes, making KDE Applications "
"friendlier and allowing you to be more productive."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:22
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>Dolphin</a> is KDE's file manager. It also connects to "
"network services, such as SSH, FTP, and Samba servers, and comes with "
"advanced tools to find and organize your data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:24
msgid "New features:"
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:27
msgid ""
"We have expanded thumbnail support, so Dolphin can now display thumbnails "
"for several new file types: <a href='%[1]s'>Microsoft Office</a> files, <a "
"href='%[2]s'>.epub and .fb2 eBook</a> files, <a href='%[3]s'>Blender</a> "
"files, and <a href='%[4]s'>PCX</a> files. Additionally, thumbnails for text "
"files now show <a href='%[5]s'>syntax highlighting</a> for the text inside "
"the thumbnail."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:29
msgid ""
"You can now choose <a href='%[1]s'>which split view pane to close</a> when "
"clicking the 'Close split' button."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:31
msgid ""
"This version of Dolphin introduces <a href='%[1]s'>smarter tab placement</"
"a>. When you open a folder in a new tab, the new tab will now be placed "
"immediately to the right of the current one, instead of always at the end of "
"the tab bar."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:33
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>Tagging items</a> is now much more practical, as tags can be "
"added or removed using the context menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:35
msgid ""
"We have <a href='%[1]s'>improved the default sorting</a> parameters for some "
"commonly-used folders. By default, the Downloads folder is now sorted by "
"date with grouping enabled, and the Recent Documents view (accessible by "
"navigating to recentdocuments:/) is sorted by date with a list view selected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:37
msgid "Bug fixes include:"
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:39
msgid ""
"When using a modern version of the SMB protocol, you can now <a "
"href='%[1]s'>discover Samba shares</a> for Mac and Linux machines."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:41
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>Re-arranging items in the Places panel</a> once again works "
"properly when some items are hidden."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:43
msgid ""
"After opening a new tab in Dolphin, that new tab's view now automatically "
"gains <a href='%[1]s'>keyboard focus</a>."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:45
msgid ""
"Dolphin now warns you if you try to quit while the <a href='%[1]s'>terminal "
"panel is open</a> with a program running in it."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:46
msgid ""
"We fixed many memory leaks, improving Dolphin's overall performance.</li>"
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:48
msgid ""
"The <a href='%[1]s'>AudioCD-KIO</a> allows other KDE applications to read "
"audio from CDs and automatically convert it into other formats."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:51
msgid "The AudioCD-KIO now supports ripping into <a href='%[1]s'>Opus</a>."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:53
msgid ""
"We made <a href='%[1]s'>CD info text</a> really transparent for viewing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:55
msgid "Video Editing"
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:59
msgid ""
"This is a landmark version for KDE's video editor. <a href='%[1]s'>Kdenlive</"
"a> has gone through an extensive re-write of its core code as more than 60%% "
"of its internals has changed, improving its overall architecture."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:64
msgid "The timeline has been rewritten to make use of QML."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:65
msgid ""
"When you put a clip on the timeline, audio and video always go to separate "
"tracks."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:66
msgid ""
"The timeline now supports keyboard navigation: clips, compositions and "
"keyframes can be moved with the keyboard. Also, the height of the tracks "
"themselves is adjustable."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:67
msgid ""
"In this version of Kdenlive, the in-track audio recording comes with a new "
"<a href='%[1]s'>voice-over</a> feature."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:68
msgid ""
"We have improved copy/paste: it works between different project windows. The "
"proxy clip management has also been enhanced, as clips can now be "
"individually deleted."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:69
msgid ""
"Version 19.04 sees the return of support for external BlackMagic monitor "
"displays and there are also new on-monitor preset guides."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:70
msgid ""
"We have improved the keyframe handling, giving it a more consistent look and "
"workflow. The titler has also been improved by making the align buttons snap "
"to safe zones, adding configurable guides and background colors, and "
"displaying missing items."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:71
msgid ""
"We fixed the timeline corruption bug that misplaced or missed clips which "
"was triggered when you moved a group of clips."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:72
msgid ""
"We fixed the JPG image bug that rendered images as white screens on Windows. "
"We also fixed the bugs affecting screen capture on Windows."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:73
msgid ""
"Apart from all of the above, we have added many small usability enhancements "
"that will make using Kdenlive easier and smoother."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:79
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>Okular</a> is KDE's multipurpose document viewer. Ideal for "
"reading and annotating PDFs, it can also open ODF files (as used by "
"LibreOffice and OpenOffice), ebooks published as ePub files, most common "
"comic book files, PostScript files, and many more."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:84
msgid ""
"To help you ensure your documents are always a perfect fit, we've added <a "
"href='%[1]s'>scaling options</a> to Okular's Print dialog."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:85
msgid ""
"Okular now supports viewing and verifying <a href='%[1]s'>digital "
"signatures</a> in PDF files."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:86
msgid ""
"Thanks to improved cross-application integration, Okular now supports "
"editing LaTeX documents in <a href='%[1]s'>TexStudio</a>."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:87
msgid ""
"Improved support for <a href='%[1]s'>touchscreen navigation</a> means you "
"will be able to move backwards and forwards using a touchscreen when in "
"Presentation mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:88
msgid ""
"Users who prefer manipulating documents from the command-line will be able "
"to perform smart <a href='%[1]s'>text search</a> with the new command-line "
"flag that lets you open a document and highlight all occurrences of a given "
"piece of text."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:89
msgid ""
"Okular now properly displays links in <a href='%[1]s'>Markdown documents</a> "
"that span more than one line."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:90
msgid "The <a href='%[1]s'>trim tools</a> have fancy new icons."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:94
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>KMail</a> is KDE's privacy-protecting email client. Part of "
"the <a href='%[2]s'>Kontact groupware suite</a>, KMail supports all email "
"systems and allows you to organize your messages into a shared virtual inbox "
"or into separate accounts (your choice). It supports all kinds of message "
"encryption and signing, and lets you share data such as contacts, meeting "
"dates, and travel information with other Kontact applications."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:99
msgid ""
"Move over, Grammarly! This version of KMail comes with support for "
"languagetools (grammar checker) and grammalecte (French-only grammar "
"checker)."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:100
msgid ""
"Phone numbers in emails are now detected and can be dialed directly via <a "
"href='%[1]s'>KDE Connect</a>."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:101
msgid ""
"KMail now has an option to <a href='%[1]s'>start directly in system tray</a> "
"without opening the main window."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:102
msgid "We have improved the Markdown plugin support."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:103
msgid "Fetching mails via IMAP no longer gets stuck when login fails."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:104
msgid ""
"We also made numerous fixes in KMail's backend Akonadi to improve "
"reliability and performance."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:106
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>KOrganizer</a> is Kontact's calendar component, managing all "
"your events."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:108
msgid ""
"Recurrent events from <a href='%[1]s'>Google Calendar</a> are again "
"synchronized correctly."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:109
msgid ""
"The event reminder window now remembers to <a href='%[1]s'>show on all "
"desktops</a>."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:110
msgid "We modernized the look of the <a href='%[1]s'>event views</a>."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:112
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>Kitinerary</a> is Kontact's brand new travel assistant that "
"will help you get to your location and advise you on your way."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:114
msgid ""
"There is a new generic extractor for RCT2 tickets (e.g. used by railway "
"companies such as DSB, ÖBB, SBB, NS)."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:115
msgid "Airport name detection and disambiguation have been greatly improved."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:116
msgid ""
"We added new custom extractors for previously unsupported providers (e.g. "
"BCD Travel, NH Group), and improved format/language variations of already "
"supported providers (e.g. SNCF, Easyjet, Booking.com, Hertz)."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:122
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>Kate</a> is KDE's full-featured text editor, ideal for "
"programming thanks to features such as tabs, split-view mode, syntax "
"highlighting, a built-in terminal panel, word completion, regular "
"expressions search and substitution, and many more via the flexible plugin "
"infrastructure."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:126
msgid "Kate can now show all invisible whitespace characters, not just some."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:127
msgid ""
"You can easily enable and disable Static Word Wrap by using its own menu "
"entry on a per-document basis, without having to change the global default "
"setting."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:128
msgid ""
"The file and tab context menus now include a bunch of useful new actions, "
"such as Rename, Delete, Open Containing Folder, Copy File Path, Compare "
"[with another open file], and Properties."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:129
msgid ""
"This version of Kate ships with more plugins enabled by default, including "
"the popular and useful inline Terminal feature."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:130
msgid ""
"When quitting, Kate no longer prompts you to acknowledge files that were "
"modified on the disk by some other process, such as a source control change."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:131
msgid ""
"The plugin’s tree view now correctly displays all menu items for git entries "
"that have umlauts in their names."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:132
msgid ""
"When opening multiple files using the command line, the files are opened in "
"new tabs in the same order as specified in the command line."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:136
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>Konsole</a> is KDE's terminal emulator. It supports tabs, "
"translucent backgrounds, split-view mode, customizable color schemes and "
"keyboard shortcuts, directory and SSH bookmarking, and many other features."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:141
msgid ""
"Tab management has seen a number of improvements that will help you be more "
"productive. New tabs can be created by middle-clicking on empty parts of the "
"tab bar, and there's also an option that allows you to close tabs by middle-"
"clicking on them. Close buttons are displayed on tabs by default, and icons "
"will be displayed only when using a profile with a custom icon. Last but not "
"least, the Ctrl+Tab shortcut allows you to quickly switch between the "
"current and previous tab."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:142
msgid ""
"The Edit Profile dialog received a huge <a href='%[1]s'>user interface "
"overhaul</a>."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:143
msgid ""
"The Breeze color scheme is now used as the default Konsole color scheme, and "
"we have improved its contrast and consistency with the system-wide Breeze "
"theme."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:144
msgid "We have resolved the issues when displaying bold text."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:145
msgid "Konsole now correctly displays the underline-style cursor."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:146
msgid ""
"We have improved the display of <a href='%[1]s'>box and line characters</a>, "
"as well as of <a href='%[2]s'>Emoji characters</a>."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:147
msgid ""
"Profile switching shortcuts now switch the current tab’s profile instead of "
"opening a new tab with the other profile."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:148
msgid ""
"Inactive tabs that receive a notification and have their title text color "
"changed now again reset the color to the normal tab title text color when "
"the tab is activated."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:149
msgid ""
"The 'Vary the background for each tab' feature now works when the base "
"background color is very dark or black."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:151
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>Lokalize</a> is a computer-aided translation system that "
"focuses on productivity and quality assurance. It is targeted at software "
"translation, but also integrates external conversion tools for translating "
"office documents."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:155
msgid ""
"Lokalize now supports viewing the translation source with a custom editor."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:156
msgid ""
"We improved the DockWidgets location, and the way settings are saved and "
"restored."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:157
msgid "The position in .po files is now preserved when filtering messages."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:158
msgid ""
"We fixed a number of UI bugs (developer comments, RegExp toggle in mass "
"replace, fuzzy empty message count, …)."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:164
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>Gwenview</a> is an advanced image viewer and organizer with "
"intuitive and easy-to-use editing tools."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:169
msgid ""
"The version of Gwenview that ships with Applications 19.04 includes full <a "
"href='%[1]s'>touchscreen support</a>, with gestures for swiping, zooming, "
"panning, and more."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:170
msgid ""
"Another enhancement added to Gwenview is full <a href='%[1]s'>High DPI "
"support</a>, which will make images look great on high-resolution screens."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:171
msgid ""
"Improved support for <a href='%[1]s'>back and forward mouse buttons</a> "
"allows you to navigate between images by pressing those buttons."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:172
msgid ""
"You can now use Gwenview to open image files created with <a "
"href='%[1]s'>Krita</a> – everyone’s favorite digital painting tool."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:173
msgid ""
"Gwenview now supports large <a href='%[1]s'>512 px thumbnails</a>, allowing "
"you to preview your images more easily."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:174
msgid ""
"Gwenview now uses the <a href='%[1]s'>standard Ctrl+L keyboard shortcut</a> "
"to move focus to the URL field."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:175
msgid ""
"You can now use the <a href='%[1]s'>Filter-by-name feature</a> with the Ctrl"
"+I shortcut, just like in Dolphin."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:179
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>Spectacle</a> is Plasma's screenshot application. You can "
"grab full desktops spanning several screens, individual screens, windows, "
"sections of windows, or custom regions using the rectangle selection feature."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:184
msgid ""
"We have extended the Rectangular Region mode with a few new options. It can "
"be configured to <a href='%[1]s'>auto-accept</a> the dragged box instead of "
"asking you to adjust it first. There is also a new default option to "
"remember the current <a href='%[2]s'>rectangular region</a> selection box, "
"but only until the program is closed."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:185
msgid ""
"You can configure what happens when the screenshot shortcut is pressed <a "
"href='%[1]s'>while Spectacle is already running</a>."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:186
msgid ""
"Spectacle allows you to change the <a href='%[1]s'>compression level</a> for "
"lossy image formats."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:187
msgid ""
"Save settings shows you what the <a href='%[1]s'>filename of a screenshot</"
"a> will look like. You can also easily tweak the <a href='%[2]s'>filename "
"template</a> to your preferences by simply clicking on placeholders."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:188
msgid ""
"Spectacle no longer displays both “Full Screen (All Monitors)” and “Current "
"Screen” options when your computer only has one screen."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:189
msgid ""
"The help text in Rectangular Region mode now shows up in the middle of the "
"primary display, rather than split between the screens."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:190
msgid "When run on Wayland, Spectacle only includes the features that work."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:192
msgid "Games and Education"
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:196
msgid ""
"Our application series includes numerous <a href='%[1]s'>games</a> and <a "
"href='%[2]s'>educational applications</a>."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:198
msgid ""
"<a href='%[1]s'>KmPlot</a> is a mathematical function plotter. It has a "
"powerful built-in parser. The graphs can be colorized and the view is "
"scalable, allowing you to zoom to the level you need. Users can plot "
"different functions simultaneously and combine them to build new functions."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:201
msgid ""
"You can now zoom in by holding down Ctrl and using the <a href='%[1]s'>mouse "
"wheel</a>."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:202
msgid ""
"This version of Kmplot introduces the <a href='%[1]s'>print preview</a> "
"option."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:204
msgid ""
"Root value or (x,y) pair can now be copied to <a href='%[1]s'>clipboard</a>."
msgstr ""

#. type: html text
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:206
msgid "<a href='%[1]s'>Kolf</a> is a miniature golf game."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:208
msgid "We have restored <a href='%[1]s'>sound support</a>."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/applications/19.04.0.md:210
msgid "Kolf has been successfully ported away from kdelibs4."
msgstr ""

