#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:0
msgid ""
"Plasma 5.21 is a looker! The new wallpaper and new app launcher make Plasma "
"not only easier on the eyes, but also easier to use and much more accessible."
msgstr ""

#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:0
msgid "We did a thing. A pretty one"
msgstr ""

#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:0
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:7
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Plasma 5"
msgid "Plasma 5.21 Beta"
msgstr "Plasma 5"

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:11
msgid ""
"Development of the upcoming version of Plasma 5.21 has, among other things, "
"introduced many improvements into Plasma's design, utilities and themes, "
"with the aim of providing end users with a more pleasant and accessible "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:15
msgid ""
"Although most things in Plasma 5.21 beta will work fine, please note it is "
"still beta software and released mainly for testing purposes. Using this "
"software in production is NOT recommended."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:17
msgid ""
"The final version of Plasma 5.21 will be available on the 16th of February."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:21
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:11
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "KDE Software Compilation 4.11 Beta1"
msgid "New Application Launcher"
msgstr "KDE-Software-Tosamenstellen 4.11 Beta 1"

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:25
msgid ""
"Plasma 5.21 introduces a new application launcher that features a double-"
"pane UI, improvements to keyboard and mouse navigation, better accessibility "
"and support for languages with RTL writing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:28
msgid ""
"The new launcher includes an alphabetical “All Applications” view, a grid-"
"style favorites view, and power actions visible by default with their labels."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:33
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:14
msgid ""
"Find, reach and run your apps faster and easier than ever with Plasma's new "
"app launcher."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:40
msgid ""
"The new launcher features two panes to make it simple to locate your "
"programs, comes with improved keyboard, mouse, and touch input, and boosts "
"the accessibility across the board. Support for languages with right-to-left "
"writing has also been improved. We have also included an alphabetical \"All "
"Applications\" view, a grid view for your favorite tools, and all the power "
"actions (\"Sleep\", \"Restart\", \"Shut Down\", etc.) are available and "
"visible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:44
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:25
msgid ""
"Last but not least, we have [fixed most of the bugs reported by users]"
"(https://invent.kde.org/plasma/plasma-desktop/-/merge_requests/258), "
"guaranteeing a smoother access to all your stuff."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:46
msgid ""
"The old Kickoff app launcher is still available at [store.kde.org](https://"
"store.kde.org)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:52
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:34
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "KDE Software Compilation 4.11 Beta1"
msgid "Application theme improvements"
msgstr "KDE-Software-Tosamenstellen 4.11 Beta 1"

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:55
msgid ""
"Applications using Plasma's default theme now have a refreshed color scheme "
"and sport a brand new unified headerbar style with a clean, cool new look."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:63
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:46
msgid "Breeze Twilight"
msgstr ""

#. type: shortcode parameter
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:65
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:48
msgid ""
"Screenshot showing Breeze Twilight with a dark panel and light applications"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:69
msgid ""
"Meet Breeze Twilight: a combination of a dark theme for Plasma and a light "
"theme for applications, so you can enjoy the best of both worlds. It's "
"available in the Global Theme settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:75
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:58
msgid ""
"![System monitor logo](https://apps.kde.org/app-icons/org.kde.plasma-"
"systemmonitor.svg)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:77
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:60
msgid "Plasma System Monitor"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:82
msgid ""
"Plasma System Monitor is a new UI for monitoring system resources. It is "
"built on top of Kirigami and a system statistics service called "
"\"KSystemStats\". It shares code with the new system monitor applets "
"introduced in Plasma 5.19 and is designed to succeed KSysGuard."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:87
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:63
msgid ""
"Plasma System Monitor is a brand new app for monitoring system resources and "
"is now an integral part of Plasma."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:94
msgid ""
"Plasma System Monitor provides many different views, offering an overview "
"page that provides information on important core resources, like memory, "
"disk space, network and CPU usage. It also provides a quick view of the "
"applications consuming the most resources."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:98
msgid ""
"If you need more details, the Applications page shows you all the running "
"applications along with detailed statistics and graphs. A process page is "
"also available for per process information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:100
msgid ""
"History shows the evolution of the use of your machine's resources over time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:103
msgid ""
"Finally, you can also create new customized pages using the page editor. "
"This lets you tailor the information you get from your system to your needs."
msgstr ""

#. type: shortcode parameter
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:109
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:83
msgid "Overview page"
msgstr ""

#. type: shortcode parameter
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:111
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:85
msgid "History page"
msgstr ""

#. type: shortcode parameter
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:113
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:87
msgid "Application resource usage overview"
msgstr ""

#. type: shortcode parameter
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:115
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:89
msgid "New page editor"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:121
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:95
msgid "KWin and Wayland"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:124
msgid ""
"KDE is pushing to have first class support for Wayland, and Plasma 5.21 "
"makes great headway to reach that goal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:129
msgid ""
"The compositing code in KWin has been extensively refactored and should "
"reduce latency throughout all compositing operations. We have also added a "
"control in the compositing settings so you can choose whether you prefer "
"lower latency or smoother animations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:133
msgid ""
"In addition, we have also added support for mixed-refresh-rate display "
"setups on Wayland, e.g. you can have one screen refreshing at 144Hz and "
"another at 60Hz. Preliminary support for multiple GPUs was also added on "
"Wayland."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:138
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:113
msgid ""
"The virtual keyboard in Wayland has been improved and now supports GTK "
"applications using the `text-input-v3` protocol. The support for graphical "
"tablets has also been improved and now includes all the controls that were "
"missing in the previous version, such as pad ring and pad buttons."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:143
msgid ""
"Apart from the numerous improvements in stability, there are quite a few "
"Plasma components that are getting much better support in Wayland. For "
"example, KRunner is now able to list all open windows in Wayland, and we now "
"support features required for GTK4, so GTK4 application will now work."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.20.90.md:149
msgid ""
"![System Settings](https://apps.kde.org/app-icons/org.kde.plasma-"
"systemmonitor.svg)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
