#. type: Title ###
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.6.95.md:31
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.7.0.md:27
msgid "Better Kiosk Support"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.6.95.md:33
msgid ""
"The <a href=\"https://userbase.kde.org/KDE_System_Administration/Kiosk/"
"Introduction\">Kiosk Framework</a> provides means of restricting the "
"customizability of the workspace, in order to keep users in an enterprise or "
"public environment from performing unwanted actions or modifications. Plasma "
"5.7 brings many corrections about enforcing such restrictions. Notably, the "
"Application Launcher will become read-only if widgets are locked through "
"Kiosk policies, i.e. favorites are locked in place and applications can no "
"longer be edited. Also, the Run Command restriction will prevent KRunner "
"from even starting in the first place."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.6.95.md:35
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.7.0.md:31
msgid "New System Tray and Task Manager"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.6.95.md:37
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.7.0.md:33
msgid ""
"The System Tray has been rewritten from scratch to allow for a simpler and "
"more maintainable codebase. While its user interface has only seen some "
"minor fixes and polishing, many issues caused by the complex nature of the "
"applet housing applets and application icons within have been resolved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.6.95.md:39
msgid ""
"Similarly, the task bar has gained a completely rewamped backend, replacing "
"the old one that has already been around in the early days of our workspace. "
"While the old backend got many features added over the period of time it was "
"used, the new one has a remarkably better performance and could be "
"engineered more cleanly and straight-forward as the requirements were known "
"beforehand. All of this will ensure a greatly increased reliability and it "
"also adds <a href=\"https://blog.martin-graesslin.com/blog/2016/06/a-task-"
"manager-for-the-plasma-wayland-session/\">support for Wayland</a> which was "
"one of the most visible omissions in our Wayland tech previews."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.6.95.md:41
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.7.0.md:37
msgid "Huge Steps Towards Wayland"
msgstr ""

#. type: shortcode parameter
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.6.95.md:43
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.7.0.md:39
msgid "Betty the Fuzzpig Tests Plasma Wayland "
msgstr ""

#. type: shortcode parameter
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.6.95.md:43
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.7.0.md:39
msgid "Betty the Fuzzpig Tests Plasma Wayland"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.6.95.md:45
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.7.0.md:41
msgid ""
"This release brings Plasma closer to the new windowing system Wayland. "
"Wayland is the successor of the decades-old X11 windowing system and brings "
"many improvements, especially when it comes to tear-free and flicker-free "
"rendering as well as security. The development of Plasma 5.7 for Wayland "
"focused on quality in the Wayland compositor KWin. Over 5,000 lines of auto "
"tests were added to KWin and another 5,000 lines were added to KWayland "
"which is now released as part of KDE Frameworks 5."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.6.95.md:47
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.7.0.md:43
msgid ""
"The already implemented workflows got stabilized and are ensured to work "
"correctly, with basic workflows now fully functional. More complex workflows "
"are not yet fully implemented and might not provide the same experience as "
"on X11. To aid debugging a new debug console got added, which can be "
"launched through KRunner using the keyword “KWin” and integrates "
"functionality known from the xprop, xwininfo, xev and xinput tools."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.6.95.md:49
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.7.0.md:45
msgid "Other improvements include:"
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.6.95.md:51
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.7.0.md:47
msgid ""
"When no hardware keyboard is connected, a <a href=\"https://blog.martin-"
"graesslin.com/blog/2016/05/virtual-keyboard-support-in-kwinwayland-5-7/"
"\">virtual keyboard</a> is shown instead, bringing a smooth converged "
"experience to tablets and convertibles"
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.6.95.md:52
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.7.0.md:48
msgid ""
"The sub-surface protocol is now supported which means that System Settings "
"works correctly and no longer errorneously opens multiple windows."
msgstr ""

#. type: List item
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.6.95.md:53
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.7.0.md:49
msgid ""
"Mouse settings, such as pointer acceleration, are honored and the touchpad "
"can be enabled/disabled through a global shortcut. Touchpad configuration is "
"still missing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain Text
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.6.95.md:55
msgid ""
"<div class=\"text-center\">{{% youtube id=\"_29BYcm8xKk\" %}}Virtual "
"Keyboard Support in Plasma Wayland</div>"
msgstr ""

